 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe other options will not give us a matrix in row echelon form." 13194139535441 17592186045443 true] [17592186262981 1071 "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535441 17592186045443 false] [17592186262981 1071 "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" 13194139535441 17592186045443 true] [17592186262981 1074 "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd rows of $A$ are $-3$, $5$, and $2$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-3+5+2=4.$" 13194139535441 17592186045443 false] [17592186262981 1074 "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd rows of $A$ are $-3$, $5$, and $2$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-3+5+2=4.$" 13194139535441 17592186045443 true] [17592186262982 1071 "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 9 & -8 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535441 17592186045443 false] [17592186262982 1071 "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 9 & -8 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 